# options = { held }; copy = Object.assign({}, options); somethingNoTableLists(copy)
# Code that nobody compiles holds the copy and reads out of it what was copied: the function has escaped. Nothing that it does to the copy is done to the source, which stays in the program.
# RUN: valueflow-why escaped=f1 escaped-layout=L0 escaped-layout=L1
# CHECK: escaped=f1
# CHECK-NEXT: n0 escaped
# CHECK: escaped-layout=L0
# CHECK-NOT: escaped
# CHECK: escaped-layout=L1
# CHECK: n0 escaped

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
layout L0 name="Options" fields=[{key="held" declared={type=anything} flags=[IsRequired]}]
layout L1 name="Copy"
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
    v0 = NewClosure function=f1
    v1 = NewObject -, v0 layout=L0 fields=[0]
    v2 = NewObject layout=L1
    v3 = Builtin builtin=Object
    v4 = Builtin builtin=ObjectAssign
    v5 = Call v4, v3, v2, v1
    v6 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v7 = PropGet v6 key="somethingThatNoTableLists" [isFreeName]
    v8 = Call v7, -, v5
    Return
}
function f1 name="held" kind=Arrow results=[{type=anything}] {
    Return
}
